Music for MUDding              NannyMUD Times                        Page 12

  After a lot of thinking, I reached a decision: mudders should listen to 
  music. I don't say that they don't listen, I just wanna tell them a few 
  suggestions, to talk about some bands and so on.

  For this month, I have chosen: "Get Cape. Wear Cape. Fly." 
  for obvious reasons.

  First thing you will see is that the name of the band is like a set of 
  commands from a MUD. Wonder if he ever played one :D. But the name comes 
  from the Essex traveller folk lore, meaning 'to live along the riverside'
  Get Cape. Wear Cape. Fly. alias Sam Duckworth alias Charlie "Charles" Khoo 
  is a half-Burmese/Vietnamese alternative musician/banter merchant born in 
  Essex. Duckworth adopted the name Get Cape. Wear Cape. Fly. in 2004 after 
  leaving his hardcore punk/Nirvana covers band Silverskin and initially 
  released records on the independent record label BSM Records, before being 
  signed to the major. He aired on BBC Radio 1 in June 2006, with his song 
  "I-Spy" being placed on the 1-Upfront list. Follow-up single "Chronicles 
  of a Bohemian Teenager (Part One)" was added to the Radio 1 and Essex 
  FM B-list. Personally, I like his song "War of the Worlds". I encourage 
  people to see the video because they will not be disapointed.

  -Bayar

